## Single: W-2 only

The API example `single-w2-50k` with $5,000 withheld (`refund-single-w2-50k`).
Calculator test `TestSingle`: wages $50,000, standard deduction $14,600, line 15
$35,400, tax $4,019 (Tax Table row $35,400 to $35,450, midpoint $35,425),
refund $5,000 - $4,019 = $981.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestApiSingle:
  d scope ApiDefaults
  output r content Api.ApiCalculator

scope TestApiSingle:
  definition r equals output of Api.ApiCalculator with {
    -- request: d.request but replace {
         -- w2s: [(output of MkApiW2 with { -- wages: $50,000 -- withholding: $5,000 }).w2] } }
  assertion r.supported
  assertion r.reasons = []
  assertion r.outcome = Api.ApiOutcome.Refund
  assertion r.lines.wages = $50,000
  assertion r.lines.agi = $50,000
  assertion r.lines.standard_or_itemized_deductions = $14,600
  assertion r.lines.taxable_income = $35,400
  assertion r.lines.total_tax = $4,019
  assertion r.lines.total_withholding = $5,000
  assertion r.lines.total_payments = $5,000
  assertion r.lines.overpayment = $981
  assertion r.lines.balance_due = $0
```

## Family with two children (MFJ)

Calculator test `TestMfj`: joint, primary wages $80,000, withholding $3,000, two
children born 2016 and 2019 with SSNs, claimed. Standard deduction $29,200,
line 15 $50,800, tax $5,635 (midpoint $50,825: 10% x $23,200 + 12% x $27,625),
child tax credit 2 x $2,000 = $4,000, total tax $1,635. No earned income credit
(2 children, joint: ends at AGI $62,688) and no additional child tax credit.
Refund $3,000 - $1,635 = $1,365. The filing status gives the defaults: married,
lived together all year.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestApiFamilyTwoKids:
  d scope ApiDefaults
  output r content Api.ApiCalculator

scope TestApiFamilyTwoKids:
  definition r equals output of Api.ApiCalculator with {
    -- request: d.request but replace {
         -- filing_status: Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
         -- dependents: [ (output of MkApiChild with { -- date_of_birth: |2016-03-01| -- upkeep: true }).child
                        ; (output of MkApiChild with { -- date_of_birth: |2019-05-01| -- upkeep: true }).child ]
         -- w2s: [(output of MkApiW2 with { -- wages: $80,000 -- withholding: $3,000 }).w2] } }
  assertion r.supported
  assertion r.lines.standard_or_itemized_deductions = $29,200
  assertion r.lines.taxable_income = $50,800
  assertion r.lines.total_tentative_tax = $5,635
  assertion r.lines.non_refundable_credits = $4,000
  assertion r.lines.total_tax = $1,635
  assertion r.lines.total_other_payments_refundable_credits = $0
  assertion r.lines.total_payments = $3,000
  assertion r.lines.overpayment = $1,365
  assertion r.outcome = Api.ApiOutcome.Refund
```

## Earned income credit and additional child tax credit (head of household)

Calculator test `TestHoh`: never married, one child born 2014 for whom the
filer paid most of the upkeep, wages $40,000, withholding $2,000. Standard
deduction $21,900, line 15 $18,100, tax $1,844 (midpoint $18,125). The child tax
credit is limited to the $1,844 of tax, so total tax is $0 and line 21 is
$1,844. Additional child tax credit $156 ($2,000 - $1,844). EIC Table, $40,000
to $40,050, one child, single or head of household: $1,448. Line 32 is
$1,448 + $156 = $1,604; payments $2,000 + $1,604 = $3,604; refund $3,604.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestApiEitcHoh:
  d scope ApiDefaults
  output r content Api.ApiCalculator

scope TestApiEitcHoh:
  definition r equals output of Api.ApiCalculator with {
    -- request: d.request but replace {
         -- filing_status: Types.FilingStatus.HeadOfHousehold
         -- dependents: [(output of MkApiChild with { -- date_of_birth: |2014-09-10| -- upkeep: true }).child]
         -- w2s: [(output of MkApiW2 with { -- wages: $40,000 -- withholding: $2,000 }).w2] } }
  assertion r.supported
  assertion r.lines.taxable_income = $18,100
  assertion r.lines.total_tentative_tax = $1,844
  assertion r.lines.non_refundable_credits = $1,844
  assertion r.lines.total_tax = $0
  assertion r.lines.total_other_payments_refundable_credits = $1,604
  assertion r.lines.total_payments = $3,604
  assertion r.lines.overpayment = $3,604
  assertion r.outcome = Api.ApiOutcome.Refund
```

## Qualifying surviving spouse: the marital defaults

Calculator test `TestQss`. The request leaves `marital_status` and
`year_of_spouse_death` unspecified: the filing status gives Widowed, died in
2023, and `can_file_jointly_year_of_spouse_death` is implied, so the status is
eligible. Wages $60,000, withholding $4,000, one child born 2012. Standard
deduction $29,200, line 15 $30,800, tax $3,235, child tax credit $2,000, total
tax $1,235, refund $4,000 - $1,235 = $2,765.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestApiQss:
  d scope ApiDefaults
  output r content Api.ApiCalculator

scope TestApiQss:
  definition r equals output of Api.ApiCalculator with {
    -- request: d.request but replace {
         -- filing_status: Types.FilingStatus.QualifyingSurvivingSpouse
         -- dependents: [(output of MkApiChild with { -- date_of_birth: |2012-02-20| -- upkeep: true }).child]
         -- w2s: [(output of MkApiW2 with { -- wages: $60,000 -- withholding: $4,000 }).w2] } }
  assertion r.supported
  assertion r.lines.taxable_income = $30,800
  assertion r.lines.total_tax = $1,235
  assertion r.lines.overpayment = $2,765
```


## Legacy flags (schema 1.0 and 1.1)

A filer who is 65 or older (`age65_or_older`, no date of birth) gets the
additional standard deduction of $1,950 (Rev. Proc. 2023-34, single): $14,600 +
$1,950 = $16,550. `filing_details.has_foreign_accounts_or_trusts` is or-ed into
the screening answer and knocks the return out.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestApiAge65:
  d scope ApiDefaults
  output r content Api.ApiCalculator

scope TestApiAge65:
  definition r equals output of Api.ApiCalculator with {
    -- request: d.request but replace {
         -- filers: Api.ApiFilers {
              -- primary: d.filer but replace { -- age65_or_older: true }
              -- secondary: d.filer }
         -- w2s: [(output of MkApiW2 with { -- wages: $50,000 -- withholding: $5,000 }).w2] } }
  assertion r.supported
  assertion r.lines.standard_or_itemized_deductions = $16,550
  assertion r.lines.taxable_income = $33,450

#[test]
declaration scope TestApiLegacyForeignAccounts:
  d scope ApiDefaults
  output r content Api.ApiCalculator

scope TestApiLegacyForeignAccounts:
  definition r equals output of Api.ApiCalculator with {
    -- request: d.request but replace {
         -- filing_details: d.request.filing_details but replace {
              -- has_foreign_accounts_or_trusts: true }
         -- w2s: [(output of MkApiW2 with { -- wages: $50,000 -- withholding: $5,000 }).w2] } }
  assertion not r.supported
  assertion r.reasons = [
    Api.ApiReason {
      -- code: Calc.CalculatorKnockout.IncomeOrHsa content KI.KnockoutReason.HasForeignAccountsOrTrusts
      -- category: AR.ApiReasonCategory.Income } ]
```

## Unsupported: reasons, their categories, and no lines

A filer who answers that Direct File does not support all of their income
sources is knocked out with exactly that reason, in the category `income`
(`api/knockout-reasons.json`). Head of household with no household member is
not an eligible status (IRC 2(b)(1)): `FilingStatusNotEligible`, category
`filers`. With both, every reason is listed, in the order of the Calculator's
knockout table (the income, HSA and process reasons first). An unsupported
return has no lines: all `$0`, outcome `Even`.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestApiUnsupportedIncome:
  d scope ApiDefaults
  output r content Api.ApiCalculator

scope TestApiUnsupportedIncome:
  definition r equals output of Api.ApiCalculator with {
    -- request: d.request but replace {
         -- w2s: [(output of MkApiW2 with { -- wages: $50,000 -- withholding: $5,000 }).w2]
         -- screening: d.request.screening but replace { -- income_sources_supported: false } } }
  assertion not r.supported
  assertion r.reasons = [
    Api.ApiReason {
      -- code: Calc.CalculatorKnockout.IncomeOrHsa content KI.KnockoutReason.IncomeSourcesNotSupported
      -- category: AR.ApiReasonCategory.Income } ]
  assertion r.outcome = Api.ApiOutcome.Even
  assertion r.lines.wages = $0
  assertion r.lines.total_tax = $0
  assertion r.lines.total_payments = $0
  assertion r.lines.overpayment = $0
  assertion r.lines.balance_due = $0

#[test]
declaration scope TestApiUnsupportedMultiple:
  d scope ApiDefaults
  output r content Api.ApiCalculator

scope TestApiUnsupportedMultiple:
  definition r equals output of Api.ApiCalculator with {
    -- request: d.request but replace {
         -- filing_status: Types.FilingStatus.HeadOfHousehold
         -- w2s: [(output of MkApiW2 with { -- wages: $50,000 -- withholding: $5,000 }).w2]
         -- screening: d.request.screening but replace { -- income_sources_supported: false } } }
  assertion not r.supported
  assertion r.reasons = [
    Api.ApiReason {
      -- code: Calc.CalculatorKnockout.IncomeOrHsa content KI.KnockoutReason.IncomeSourcesNotSupported
      -- category: AR.ApiReasonCategory.Income };
    Api.ApiReason {
      -- code: Calc.CalculatorKnockout.Household content KI.KnockoutReason.ExtraFilingStatusNotEligible
      -- category: AR.ApiReasonCategory.Household } ]
  assertion r.lines.total_income = $0
```

## The category of a reason

One constructor of each kind: an income-or-HSA reason (the category is that of
the inner reason), and the reasons the other modules add.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestApiReasonCategories:
  c1 scope AR.ApiReasonCategoryOf
  c2 scope AR.ApiReasonCategoryOf
  c3 scope AR.ApiReasonCategoryOf
  c4 scope AR.ApiReasonCategoryOf
  c5 scope AR.ApiReasonCategoryOf
  output ok condition

scope TestApiReasonCategories:
  definition c1.reason equals
    Calc.CalculatorKnockout.IncomeOrHsa content KI.KnockoutReason.FlowKnockoutHasBonds
  definition c2.reason equals Calc.CalculatorKnockout.Household content KI.KnockoutReason.ExtraTpNeedsToAdd1095A
  definition c3.reason equals Calc.CalculatorKnockout.Household content KI.KnockoutReason.ExtraFilingStatusNotEligible
  definition c4.reason equals Calc.CalculatorKnockout.Household content KI.KnockoutReason.ExtraQualifyingChildTieBreaker
  definition c5.reason equals Calc.CalculatorKnockout.Household content KI.KnockoutReason.SaversCreditKnockouts
  rule ok under condition
    c1.category = AR.ApiReasonCategory.Interest
    and c2.category = AR.ApiReasonCategory.HealthCoverage
    and c3.category = AR.ApiReasonCategory.Household
    and c4.category = AR.ApiReasonCategory.Household
    and c5.category = AR.ApiReasonCategory.Credits
  consequence fulfilled
  assertion ok
```

## The outcome

`Refund` if line 34 is positive, `BalanceDue` if line 37 is positive, else
`Even`; for a return Form 1040 never has both. The test also rejects the wrong
outcome for each case.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestApiOutcomes:
  a scope Api.OutcomeOf
  b scope Api.OutcomeOf
  c scope Api.OutcomeOf
  output ok condition

scope TestApiOutcomes:
  definition a.overpayment equals $981
  definition a.balance_due equals $0
  definition b.overpayment equals $0
  definition b.balance_due equals $619
  definition c.overpayment equals $0
  definition c.balance_due equals $0
  rule ok under condition
    a.outcome = Api.ApiOutcome.Refund and a.outcome != Api.ApiOutcome.BalanceDue
    and b.outcome = Api.ApiOutcome.BalanceDue and b.outcome != Api.ApiOutcome.Refund
    and c.outcome = Api.ApiOutcome.Even and c.outcome != Api.ApiOutcome.Refund
  consequence fulfilled
  assertion ok
```

## The spec rejects wrong outputs

Known-bad outputs for the single return above: the tax without the Tax Table
midpoint ($35,400 x rates = $4,016), the refund with the standard deduction
left out, and a balance due where the filer overpaid.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestApiRejectsBadOutputs:
  s scope TestApiSingle
  output ok condition

scope TestApiRejectsBadOutputs:
  rule ok under condition
    s.r.lines.total_tax != $4,016 and s.r.lines.overpayment != $0
    and s.r.lines.agi != $35,400 and s.r.lines.balance_due != $981
    and s.r.outcome != Api.ApiOutcome.BalanceDue and s.r.supported
  consequence fulfilled
  assertion ok
```
